      "lineNbr": 253,
      "author": {
        "id": 1916
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-02-16T19:36:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, that\u0027s how it is being setup in devstack right now. You can either use the legacy URL or\n\n/identity/v3\n/identity/v2.0\n/identity_admin/v3\n/identity_admin/v2.0\n\nSee\n\nhttps://github.com/openstack-dev/devstack/blob/master/files/apache-keystone.template#L38\n\nIn fact, that\u0027s the direction we are heading, that we are using the standard HTTP/S ports and namespace each service in the SCRIPT_NAME. That way, we don\u0027t have to worry non-standard ports in production deployment. Much easier to deal with the networking and security folks.",
      "parentUuid": "dae33548_0a487b2c",
      "revId": "1b29e3fb59ecf8574451e5a985cb687eb24faf5b",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
